    "narrative": "For July 3rd, the LawDog lineup is headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jonathan Aranda** (68.46), who represent our highest-upside plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter against Tyler Phillips, leveraging a high base projection bolstered by a significant +13% platoon edge and a +10% park factor. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is in a prime position to produce against the vulnerable Spencer Arrighetti; his elite 0.378 xwOBA is supported by a +12% platoon boost and an advantageous #2 spot in the order. We are also heavily capitalizing on the Coors Field factor, as **Luis Arraez**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** all see their scores elevated by a massive +14% park adjustment, making them strong starts despite varying spots in the lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Geraldo Perdomo**, who landed at 49.92. While his #2 batting order projection offered a boost, he was ultimately pushed out by the higher floor provided by our current infield configuration and the fact that he faces Kyle Harrison, an elite arm with a sub-3.00 xERA. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh** (41.82); while he is active, he faces the toughest assignment of the day in Dylan Cease. His score is suppressed by a negative SP skill adjustment and park factors, placing him firmly in the marginal category. Users should note that these rankings are based on \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters; monitor team news closely, as any deviation in batting order for **Yainer Diaz** or **Masyn Winn** could necessitate a recalibration of our efficiency expectations for the evening.",
